## Scanner v2 — Cup & Handle Added

### New Features Added

- **Cup & Handle pattern detection** on the RS line curve
- **Pattern badges**: ☕ C&H (full pattern), ◡ Cup (forming, no handle yet)
- **RS Line sparkline** — mini SVG chart showing the actual RS line shape per stock
- **Pattern quality score** (0–100 ring) based on O’Neil criteria
- **C&H Only toggle** — filter to show only stocks with a complete Cup & Handle
- **C&H Details column**: cup depth %, handle depth/weeks, cup duration in weeks

### Cup & Handle Detection Rules (O’Neil Criteria)

```
Cup:
  - Depth: 10–40% (ideal: 12–25%)
  - Duration: minimum 5 weeks (ideal 7–26 weeks)
  - Right rim must recover to ≥85% of left rim height
  - Smooth, rounded "U" shape preferred over "V"

Handle:
  - Retracement: 2–12% from right rim (ideal ≤8%)
  - Duration: 1–7 weeks
  - Must form in upper half of the cup (above midpoint)
  - Volume should dry up during handle formation

Pivot Point:
  - The right rim of the cup = breakout price
  - Buy within 5% above the pivot on volume
```

### Pattern Quality Score Breakdown

|Criteria                                      |Points |
|----------------------------------------------|-------|
|Cup detected (valid depth + duration)         |+40    |
|Handle detected (valid retracement + location)|+30    |
|Ideal cup depth (12–25%)                      |+10    |
|Right rim ≥95% of left rim                    |+10    |
|Handle retracement ≤8%                        |+5     |
|Cup duration 7–26 weeks                       |+5     |
|**Maximum score**                             |**100**|

