## How the RS Line Works

### Calculation

```
Step 1: Get 52 weekly closing prices for the stock
Step 2: Get 52 weekly closing prices for SPY (S&P 500 ETF)
Step 3: RS Ratio[i] = Stock Close[i] ÷ SPY Close[i]
Step 4: Normalise: divide all values by the first ratio
        → First point = 1.0, subsequent points show relative performance
Step 5: RS Line 52-week high = max value over all 52 points
Step 6: RS vs 52-week high = Current RS ÷ RS 52-week high × 100
```

### RS Rating (Percentile Rank)

- Ranks each stock against the entire scan universe
- Score of 99 = top 1% performer in the universe
- Score of 70 = outperforms 70% of all stocks scanned
- Colour coding: ≥90 bright green, ≥75 green, ≥60 amber, <60 red

### What to Look For

|Signal                                |Meaning                   |Action                     |
|--------------------------------------|--------------------------|---------------------------|
|RS line new 52-wk high, price in base |Institutions buying early |**Highest priority setup** |
|RS line new high on price breakout    |Confirms breakout         |Buy on breakout with volume|
|RS line flat while price rises        |Rising only with market   |Lower conviction           |
|RS line falling while price holds     |Relative weakness — danger|Avoid or exit              |
|RS line breaks below RS line base lows|Leadership lost           |Exit immediately           |

