## Quick Reference Decision Table

|Location  |Trigger               |Volume   |RS Line  |Action      |
|----------|----------------------|---------|---------|------------|
|Near pivot|Break PDH             |High     |New high |✅ Full buy  |
|Near pivot|Break PDH             |Low      |Flat     |⚠️ Wait/small|
|Near pivot|Fails at pivot        |Any      |Declining|Reduce      |
|Mid-base  |Break intra-base pivot|High     |Rising   |Half buy    |
|Mid-base  |Chop                  |Drying up|New high |Hold/watch  |
|Support   |Undercut & reclaim    |High     |Holds    |✅ Strong buy|
|Support   |Break below           |High     |Breaking |❌ Exit      |
|Any       |Gap below base        |Any      |Collapses|❌ Sell all  |

-----

## The #1 Rule

> **The RS Line leads price.**
> 
> If the RS line is making new highs before the price breakout, you have early confirmation from institutional money flow. If the RS line is failing while price holds, get out before the crowd does.

